  "result": "Fixed. The command now prints `27.06`.\n\n**Root cause:** `to_cents` in `shop/money.py` padded the decimal part on the wrong side. It used `frac.rjust(2, \"0\")`, so `\"12.5\"` became `\"12.05\"` and was read as 1205 cents instead of 1250. The correct padding is `ljust`, which turns `\"5\"` into `\"50\"`.\n\nWith that change, 2 \u00d7 $12.50 = $25.00, plus 8.25% tax ($2.0625, rounded to $2.06), gives `27.06`.\n\n**Tests:** pytest isn't installed here, so I ran them with `python3 -m unittest discover`. All 6 pass.",
